  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Spiritibus.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">Literis, praesertim vocalibus, accidit</l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Spiritus</i> inscriptus: qui est</l>
    <l n="4">vel Asper, vel Lenis.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Asperi spiritus (qui etiam Densus</l>
    <l n="6">vocatur) nota est, in majusculis in mi-</l>
    <l n="7">nusculis . ut: <i>Ἁμαρτία, ἁμαρτάνω.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">Lenis spiritus (qui &amp; Tenuis) nota</l>
    <l n="9">est, in majusculis <i>'</i>, in minusculis <i>'</i>. ut:</l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Ἀρχὴ, ἐγώ.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">REGVLAE. I. Omnis Vocalis &amp;</l>
    <l n="12">Diphthongus, à principio dictionis, al-</l>
    <l n="13">terutrum e spiritibus inscriptum habet,</l>
    <l n="14">&amp; quidem perpetuò densum.</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">II. Consonans <i>ρ</i>, dictionem inco-</l>
    <l n="16">hās, semper aspiratur. ut: <i>ῥέω.</i> In medio</l>
    <l n="17">autem dictionis, si geminetur: prius <i>ρ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">levigatur; posterius aspiratur. ut: <i>ἐρρῆ-κα, ῥόππω.</i>]</l>
    <l n="19" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Apostropho.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">
      <i>Apostrophus</i>, est nota abjectae Vocalis</l>
    <l n="21">aut Diphthongi, in fine dictionis, ob se-</l>
    <l n="22">quentis vocalem aut diphthongum in-</l>
    <l n="23">itialem. ut: <i>ταῦτ' ἔλεγον</i>, pro, <i>ταῦτα ἔλεγον:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>βιβλίον' ἐγώ</i>, pro, <i>βιβλίου ἐγώ.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Abjiciuntur autem, ex Vocalibus,</l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>α, ε, ι, ο</i>: ex Diphthongis, <i>αι, &amp; οι.</i>
    </l>
